  "implementation": "A separate finite Flow section represents the rank-one map at a tangent-aligned up direction; Frame3 remains orthonormal. Exact-zero crosses collapse both transverse axes, while nonzero crosses retain their direction. Roadlike Rigid retains the original pose when its placement frame is degenerate, and propagates nonfinite/other failures. Three-point arcs reuse public OpenNURBS construction after tolerance checks, retaining a scaled Rust fallback outside the native constructor range. Curve evaluation uses the supporting-plane angular interval and the public OpenNURBS quadrant cleanup, including reversed arcs. GNU/Clang native builds disable multiply/add contraction to preserve operation boundaries. A native unit regression retains the formerly tilted coordinate-axis frame.",
